<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Our algorithm operates on the augmented distribution underlying the
proximal sampler of Lee, Shen, and Tian <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>. For a
scale <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1/\beta]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1/\beta]</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the joint law</p>
<table id="S2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\|x-y\|^{2}}{2\eta}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y)\propto\exp\Bigl\{-V(x)-\frac{\|x-y\|^{2}}{2\eta}\Bigr\}\,\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}y\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The original proximal sampler algorithm performs Gibbs sampling on <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Namely, under <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> one may generate the joint state as</p>
<table id="S2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\sim\mu\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\ \text{independently}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>independently</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\sim\mu\,,\hskip 20.00003ptZ\sim\mathcal{N}(0,I)\ \text{independently}\,,\hskip 20.00003ptY=X+\sqrt{\eta}\,Z\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
